  "license_note": "Values from the INSPIRE registry. Colours: default style LandUse.ExistingLandUse.Default of the Land Use Technical Guidelines, section 11.2 (https://inspire-mif.github.io/technical-guidelines/data/lu/dataspecification_lu.html): six level-1 fills plus five permitted adjustments (1_1, 1_2, 4_1_4, 6_3_1, 6_3_2); the guideline's style table spells four of them differently (style_name).",
  "key": "code",
  "fields": {"code": ["hilucslanduse", "hilucs", "hilucs_value", "hilucsvalue", "hilucs_code"]},
  "hierarchy": "prefix",
  "note": "Keys are the numeric part of the registry value, with underscores (3_4_3); name holds the full value (3_4_3_SportsInfrastructure). The separator is an underscore, not a dot, so the scheme uses the prefix fallback: a full value such as 3_4_3_SportsInfrastructure (or the style-table spelling 4_1_4_WaterTraffic) sheds characters until it reaches 3_4_3, and an unlisted 3_2_1 falls back to 3_2. Full registry URIs (http://inspire.ec.europa.eu/codelist/HILUCSValue/...) must be cut to the value first. Six registry values are not listed because the research does not name them (2_3_5 and 3_2_1 to 3_2_5); they resolve to 2_3 and 3_2. HILUCS is land use: the drawing is the nearest land-use element and says nothing about cover. Only level 1 and the five adjusted values carry colours; the default style fills every other value with the colour of its level-1 group.",
